Package: datakit
Title: Grouped Assignment and Labelled Columns for Data Preparation
Version: 0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jbearak@guttmacher.org")
Description: Data preparation in R. d[i, name, by = g] := value makes or
    changes a column of a data frame or tibble for the rows i, within
    groups g, as one line of a do-file does. Columns with value labels
    keep them, and keep the extended missing values .a to .z as tagged
    NAs, without haven or dtaparser loaded: their class puts datakit's
    rules first and haven's class second, so integer codes become
    doubles when they must hold .a to .z or a fraction, and haven's
    functions still read the columns.
License: GPL-3
